{"tool_name":"spot-rna","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"SPOT-RNA","home":"http://sparks-lab.org/jaswinder/server/SPOT-RNA/","summary":"RNA secondary structure predictor","addition_date":"2019-12-25T03:46:00Z","last_update_date":"2021-09-28T10:47:18.113882Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:SPOT-RNA","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"jaswinder.singh3@griffithuni.edu.au","name":"Jaswinder Singh","note":"PhD Candidate at Signal Processing Lab, Griffith University","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0478-5533","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"http://sparks-lab.org"}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"https://github.com/jaswindersingh2/SPOT-RNA/blob/master/README.md"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"RNA sequence","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_3495"},"format":[{"term":"FASTA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1929"}]}],"operation":[{"term":"RNA secondary structure prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0278"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"RNA secondary structure","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_0880"}}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"SPOT-RNA","operating_system":["Linux"],"owner":"jaswinder_singh","publication":[{"doi":"10.1038/s41467-019-13395-9","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2019, The Author(s).The majority of our human genome transcribes into noncoding RNAs with unknown structures and functions. Obtaining functional clues for noncoding RNAs requires accurate base-pairing or secondary-structure prediction. However, the performance of such predictions by current folding-based algorithms has been stagnated for more than a decade. Here, we propose the use of deep contextual learning for base-pair prediction including those noncanonical and non-nested (pseudoknot) base pairs stabilized by tertiary interactions. Since only < 250 nonredundant, high-resolution RNA structures are available for model training, we utilize transfer learning from a model initially trained with a recent high-quality bpRNA dataset of > 10,000 nonredundant RNAs made available through comparative analysis. The resulting method achieves large, statistically significant improvement in predicting all base pairs, noncanonical and non-nested base pairs in particular. The proposed method (SPOT-RNA), with a freely available server and standalone software, should be useful for improving RNA structure modeling, sequence alignment, and functional annotations.","authors":[{"name":"Hanson J."},{"name":"Paliwal K."},{"name":"Singh J."},{"name":"Zhou Y."}],"citationCount":38,"date":"2019-12-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nature Communications","title":"RNA secondary structure prediction using an ensemble of two-dimensional deep neural networks and transfer learning"},"pmcid":"PMC6881452","pmid":"31776342","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Nucleic acid structure analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0097"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"SPOT-RNA","home":"https://bio.tools/SPOT-RNA","summary":"RNA secondary structure predictor","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:spot-rna/cmd/sparks-lab.org","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":null,"registration":null},"packages":null,"source_packages":false,"sourcecode":{"free":true,"interpreted":true,"license":true,"public":true,"readme":true,"repository":{"anonymous":true,"online":true}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"manual":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":175,"citations":[{"count":8,"year":"2020"},{"count":15,"year":"2021"},{"count":15,"year":"2026"},{"count":29,"year":"2023"},{"count":32,"year":"2024"},{"count":35,"year":"2022"},{"count":41,"year":"2025"}],"doi":"10.1038/s41467-019-13395-9","pm